[Debug] ----- Vuln Cause Analysis -----
The potential vulnerability is related to an Uncontrolled Resource Consumption vulnerability, often referred to as a Denial of Service (DoS) attack. This vulnerability arises from the lack of validation on the size and content of the uploaded zip files. If the API does not impose limits on the size of the zip file or the number of files it can contain, an attacker could upload excessively large zip files or a large number of files, leading to resource exhaustion on the server. This could result in degraded performance or complete unavailability of the service, as the server may become overwhelmed by the processing demands of handling such inputs.

